course: dictionary
lesson: 15307
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Slew is one of those words. Read the words around it, then ask: what would fit here?
explain: «A slew of emails arrived in my inbox this morning.» A slew of means a large number, so there were lots of emails. The emails tell you this is not about turning or killing.
explain: «The bike hit a patch of ice and slewed sideways across the road.» Slewed means turned or slid sideways suddenly, out of control. The ice and the skid are the clues.
explain: «The brave knight slew the dragon.» Here slew is the old past form of slay, so it means killed. You will mostly find it in old stories. To check, swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Slew has several meanings, so always check the context.
fact: «A slew of» means a large number or amount of things. It is informal, so you will hear it in everyday talk.
fact: «Slewed» means turned or slid sideways suddenly, often in a car, bike or boat.
fact: «Slew» is the old past form of «slay», meaning killed, as in «the knight slew the dragon».
fact: If the context still leaves you unsure, check a dictionary.
exercise: «A slew of new games arrived in the shop.» What does a slew of mean here? | A kind of fish | A loud noise from | *A large number of | A tiny piece of
exercise: «The car hit the ice and slewed sideways across the road.» What does slewed mean? | Stopped very slowly and politely | Shone brightly in the sun | Sang loudly as it drove | *Turned or slid sideways suddenly and out of control
exercise: «The hero slew the monster in the old tale.» Which word means the same as slew here? | ran | sang | *killed | hid
test: What does «a slew of» mean in «a slew of questions»? | *A large number | A kind of question | Very cold | A small number
test: «The knight slew the dragon and saved the village.» What does slew mean here? | Shone brightly | Turned sideways | *Killed, the old past form of slay | Shouted loudly
exam: Which sentence uses slewed to mean skidded sideways? | «The bus stopped for a rest.» | «The bus slowly parked by the school.» | *«The bus slewed round the corner on the icy road.» | «The bus was a slew of colours.»
